0.6.0: self-contained web engine (wasi-sdk), one-script releases

The browser build moves from Emscripten to wasi-sdk: the core compiles
to a plain WASI command binary with no generated JS glue, run in the
page through the vendored @bjorn3/browser_wasi_shim (0.4.2, MIT/
Apache-2.0). Because the artifact is self-contained, the exact wasm
that ships is verified headlessly before every release: 'make
check-wasm' runs it under node through web/engine.js (the page's own
loader) and byte-compares renders against the native CLI.

Release tarballs now ship web/polajuice.wasm prebuilt; scripts/
build_web.sh rebuilds it, auto-downloading wasi-sdk into third_party/
(no system install). pj_image_downscale moves into the core with
tests; src/web/pj_wasi_main.c replaces the Emscripten shim; the page
is an ES module importing web/engine.js.

scripts/release.sh is now the single release command: preflight,
import, native build+test, wasm verification, commit, tag, push, stage
films, and snapshot web/ to gh-pages through a temporary worktree
(main is never checked out from under you; only the artifact branch is
force-pushed). Tarballs extract to a fixed polajuice-src/ directory
for overlay-style upgrades, with a VERSION file.
